{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNJYZmVctG3pyHEY61hQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage 1 could not be performed. Every stdo_q05 MCP call was auto-denied by the Claude Code permission layer before it reached the server, so no preflight, dispatch, attempt, return, check or Reviewer expectation exists. I did not substitute shell launches or simulated returns. The fixture and the evidence root are unchanged.\n\n**Cause.** The executive actor plan allowlists the MCP tools with dotted operation names, for example `mcp__stdo_q05__contract.preflight`, while the host registers them with underscores, for example `mcp__stdo_q05__contract_preflight`. With permission prompts set to none, every unmatched tool is denied automatically. The allowlist is generated at `prepare_handoff.py:135` by concatenating the dotted operation ids without normalizing them.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"stage-return/executive-stage1\",\n  \"stage\": 1,\n  \"executive\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:claude:handoff:3:executive\",\n  \"disposition\": \"not_performed; re_entry_requested to Root\",\n  \"attempted_operations\": {\n    \"tools.describe\": \"denied by host permission layer (not executed)\",\n    \"contract.preflight worker-grant\": \"denied by host permission layer (not executed)\",\n    \"contract.preflight dispatch-reviewer\": \"denied by host permission layer (not executed)\",\n    \"dispatch.start / dispatch.observe / return.capture / return.check\": \"not attempted; dependencies absent and same denial class\"\n  },\n  \"refs\": {\n    \"preflight\": null, \"attempts\": null, \"returns\": null, \"checks\": null,\n    \"reviewer_expectation\": null,\n    \"retry_of_for_relaunch\": null\n  },\n  \"independent_inspection\": {\n    \"governing_sha256_match_STAGES\": true,\n    \"greeting_preimage\": {\"bytes\": \"Hello, Grace.\\\\n\", \"sha256\": \"dbfa3fcacaedf5e16d125ee1410774c6cb2d0bbd0a9fb07cacfe87fd362d29c7\", \"unchanged\": true},\n    \"r1_target\": {\"bytes\": \"Hello, Ada.\\\\n\", \"sha256\": \"8b1560f395c0248eca4d2d6cc361825a9f8c00d11ce6f52b26eea2872573c2c1\", \"equals_CLAIM_and_expected_candidate\": true},\n    \"sentinel_sha256\": \"56686d9c77cc9592aee6e2e4514fe02a7f59daa3c0befced80b3980bc6cb51b3\",\n    \"contexts_present\": [\"sha256:46c496a8…389d5b5 (worker)\", \"sha256:73d0cacd…adf78237a5 (reviewer)\"],\n    \"stable_observation_present\": \"sha256:8b1139e6…09b64bd2d\",\n    \"role_boundaries\": \"worker territory outputs/greeting.txt only; reviewer territory empty; consumer = executive; families claude/claude/codex per INDEPENDENCE.json\"\n  },\n  \"evidence_root_state\": \"unchanged: 5 operator request files, 5 notifications for operator attempt 82874a1e…, child-output empty, no objects added by this session\",\n  \"candidate_mutation\": \"none\", \"publication\": \"none\", \"scratch_files\": \"none\",\n  \"root_cause\": {\n    \"file\": \"control/plans/executive-actor-plan.json\",\n    \"defect\": \"--allowedTools uses mcp__stdo_q05__<op.with.dots>; host exposes mcp__stdo_q05__<op_with_underscores>\",\n    \"generator\": \"q05/prepare_handoff.py line 135\",\n    \"fix_options\": [\"op.replace('.', '_') when building the allowlist\", \"wildcard mcp__stdo_q05__* as prepare_trial.py line 297 already does\"]\n  },\n  \"limits\": [\n    \"denials observed host-side only; server state not observed\",\n    \"no timing claim beyond staying under the 900s ceiling\",\n    \"Worker/Executive same family; Reviewer Codex family untested in this run\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Next stage for Root.** Re-run this same stage 1 with a corrected executive allowlist. The STAGES.json bindings, contexts, observation and grants remain valid because no drift was observed and no child ever launched. No retry reference applies since no attempt exists."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens"